					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calamityheart" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1973848); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1973848&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380423" alt="CalamityHeart" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1973848)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/calamityheart" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1973848); return false;" >CalamityHeart</a></span> <span class="odate time_1525261667 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 May 2018 11:47</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3787444">
									

<p>This is creepy-good.</p>
<p>Things like this, that give anomalous context to mundane real-life phenomena, are some of my favorites to read, and it's used to great effect here.</p>
<p>Well-written throughout, and I enjoyed the last addendum's conservation of mystery. I can see what the guy did, but I can't really tell <em>what</em> he did, or what's actually happening to him, which lets my imagination wander. Some puzzle pieces are there, but putting them together is challenging.</p>
<p>My personal interpretation is that he tried to put himself into a television show somehow with an anomalous tool, but it didn't quite work, and instead of passing through the fourth wall, his soul stopped <em>inside</em> it, and only a small part of 'him', his raw sense of humor, was able to pull all the way through and react to the funny-funny of the stuff in TV-land. This was fine with him at first. If this was as close as he could get to being a part of a television show, so be it. It was funny, and he wanted to be closer to that funny. How was he to know that a raw personality trait, when exposed to others without being naturally buffered by <em>other</em> personality traits, was hazardous to mental health?</p>
<p>Then one day, there was some kind of accident with his device. His soul kind of snapped off, and his body died completely, while his soul became irreversibly stuck inside the fourth wall. Then it <em>stopped</em> being funny.</p>
<p>That's probably all wrong. xD But it's fun to think and muse about stuff like this.</p>
<p>Good job! Hearty +1!</p>

							</div>

								
					
