			<div class="content" id="post-content-3812307">
									

<p>Ah, this is giving me chills. I had a playlist in the background as I read it, and I nearly jumped when I heard something vaguely like laughing. The imagery of the face mask with laughing gas was, ugh. I was going to pass this off as spooky without meaning behind it at first, but reading the comments made me take a second look.</p>
<p>I'm thinking that the subjects become something like actors in a sitcom, hearing laugh tracks from the left or right (presumably where the live audience would be). Talico had a magic broadcaster that would add a laugh track (that would infect humans who heard it long enough) if a show didn't already have one, is my take.</p>
<p>I like how this explains why comedies all have those darn laugh tracks nowadays.</p>

